      {
        "id": "p14-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "By adding and subtracting $4x^2$, factorise $x^4+4$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x^2+2-2x)(x^2+2+2x)$\n\nForm a perfect square, then use the difference of two squares.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^4+4&=x^4+4x^2+4-4x^2\\\\x^4+4&=(x^2+2)^2-(2x)^2\\\\x^4+4&=(x^2+2-2x)(x^2+2+2x)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p14-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Factorise $x^4+4a^4$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x^2+2a^2-2ax)(x^2+2a^2+2ax)$\n\nAdd and subtract $4a^2x^2$, then use the difference of two squares.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^4+4a^4&=x^4+4a^2x^2+4a^4-4a^2x^2\\\\x^4+4a^4&=(x^2+2a^2)^2-(2ax)^2\\\\x^4+4a^4&=(x^2+2a^2-2ax)(x^2+2a^2+2ax)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
  },
